 ## Background
-UE4-NeRF was introduced in the paper "UE4-NeRF: Neural Radiance Field for Real-Time Rendering of Large-Scale Scene" [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of existing NeRF methods in real-time rendering of large-scale scenes, such as high training costs, slow rendering speeds, and lack of editability. The method combines NeRF with the Unreal Engine 4 (UE4) rasterization pipeline, leveraging LOD techniques and multi-resolution hash encoding to achieve real-time performance. It is used in UE4 for real-time interactive rendering and scene editing/manipulation, particularly for drone-captured large-scale scenes like farmlands, construction sites, and industrial parks, and has been evaluated on the Mega-NeRF public dataset [S1].
+UE4-NeRF was introduced in the paper "UE4-NeRF: Neural Radiance Field for Real-Time Rendering of Large-Scale Scene" [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of existing NeRF methods in real-time rendering of large-scale scenes, such as high training costs, slow rendering speeds, and lack of editability [S1]. The method combines NeRF with the Unreal Engine 4 (UE4) rasterization pipeline, leveraging LOD techniques and multi-resolution hash encoding to achieve real-time performance [S1]. It is used in UE4 for real-time interactive rendering and scene editing/manipulation, particularly for drone-captured large-scale scenes like farmlands, construction sites, and industrial parks, and has been evaluated on the Mega-NeRF public dataset [S1].
 
